<!--
  Wazuh <localfile> for the nightly maintenance status line written by
  main.sh on the Pi-hole VM, wazuh-home and (once it has an agent) the
  edge VPS. Not for the Vault VM, which has vault-maint-agent.localfile.xml.

  Append to /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf on that host, then restart:
      Pi-hole VM / VPS:  sudo systemctl restart wazuh-agent
      wazuh-home:        sudo systemctl restart wazuh-manager
  Check:
      sudo grep maint-status /var/ossec/logs/ossec.log | tail -2
      # expect: Analyzing file: '/var/log/maint-status.jsonl'

  If the file doesn't exist yet (before the first run), create it empty
  first, so the agent starts reading it right away:
      sudo touch /var/log/maint-status.jsonl

  A single, non-dated file on purpose: the agent keeps its read position
  in it, so the line written seconds before a reboot still ships (a new
  dated file each day isn't picked up in time). Rotated with copytruncate
  by logrotate-maint-status.
-->
<ossec_config>
  <localfile>
    <log_format>json</log_format>
    <location>/var/log/maint-status.jsonl</location>
  </localfile>
</ossec_config>
